  "weight_rates_source_url": "https://pe.usps.com/text/dmm300/Notice123.pdf",
  "cubic": {
    "exists_after_july_2026": true,
    "eligibility": "Commercial only: eligible USPS Ground Advantage - Commercial customers, including Ground Advantage Return service customers, under DMM 505.3.0 (DMM 283.1.3.1). Commercial prices require a qualifying payment method (DMM 283.1.2): registered PC Postage end users with a qualifying label, USPS-approved IBI meters, permit imprint, or Returns service for permit holders. In practice small sellers reach it through PC Postage platforms; which specific platforms offer it was not verified this round. Each piece: 1 cubic foot or less, 20 lb or less, longest dimension 22 in or less (raised from 18 in effective 2026-07-12). Rolls and tubes are not eligible.",
    "measurement_rule": "Measure L, W, H in inches at the maximum point of each dimension, round each DOWN to the nearest 1/4 inch, multiply L x W x H and divide by 1,728 to get cubic feet. Ten tiers in 0.10 cu ft steps (0.10 to 1.00); a piece falls in the smallest tier whose value it does not exceed, i.e. tier = ceil(cu_ft / 0.1) * 0.1. DMM example: 6 x 5.75 x 6.25 in = 0.125 cu ft, which is Tier 0.20 (DMM 283.1.3.2-1.3.3).",
    "soft_pack_rule": "Soft packs and padded envelopes (DMM 283.1.3.4, Exhibit 1.3.4, revised 2026-07-12 to five tiers matching Priority Mail Cubic soft pack): use the outside dimensions of the original packaging, length and width only (height ignored), each rounded DOWN to the nearest 1/4 inch, then added. L+W must not exceed 36 in. Tiers by L+W: up to 21 in = 0.10; over 21 up to 27 = 0.20; over 27 up to 31 = 0.30; over 31 up to 34 = 0.40; over 34 up to 36 = 0.50. Pleated or expandable pieces must also meet the 1.3.3 measurement rules.",
