    "post_2027_01_17": "not_found. The USPS holiday release (https://about.usps.com/newsroom/national-releases/2026/0825-usps-announces-temporary-price-change-for-2026-holiday-shipping-season.pdf, primary) gives only the end date, not post-period prices. Supply Chain Dive (secondary) reports a USPS fuel surcharge starting January 2027 as a weekly-adjusted percentage of base postage covering Ground Advantage; exact start date and post-Jan-17 base prices not found.",
    "notes": "Two separate reads of the p.16 table agreed on every cell. Zone 9 equals Zone 8 in every tier. Cubic prices are not shown for zone 1&2 combined; zones 1 and 2 are separate. The Notice footnotes on p.16 list the package quality noncompliance fee, nonstandard characteristic surcharge, live animal and HAZMAT fees. Cubic is cheaper than weight pricing for dense small items: e.g., Zone 5, a 2.5 lb candle in a 0.2 cu ft box is $9.92 cubic vs $12.12 (3 lb) weight-based."
